6:["$","$1","c",{"children":[["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","header",null,{"className":"bg-gradient-to-br from-eng-navy-900 to-eng-navy-700","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"container mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-12 sm:py-16","children":[["$","nav",null,{"aria-label":"Breadcrumb","className":"mb-6 text-sm text-white/80","children":[["$","$L9",null,{"href":"/eng0300","className":"hover:text-white","children":"ENG0300"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"mx-2","aria-hidden":"true","children":"/"}],["$","$L9",null,{"href":"/eng0300/tabe","className":"hover:text-white","children":"TABE Prep"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"mx-2","aria-hidden":"true","children":"/"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"font-medium text-white","children":"Language"}]]}],["$","h1",null,{"className":"font-display text-3xl font-bold text-white sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl","children":"TABE Language Prep"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-3 max-w-[62ch] text-base leading-relaxed text-white/90 sm:text-lg","children":"The Language subtest is not a grammar quiz in the abstract. It gives you sentences and short passages in ordinary adult contexts and asks you to fix them, finish them, or judge them — editing work, presented the way editing actually happens."}],["$","$L9",null,{"href":"/eng0300/tabe","className":"mt-5 inline-block rounded-lg bg-white/15 px-4 py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-white hover:bg-white/25 focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-white focus-visible:ring-offset-2 focus-visible:ring-offset-eng-navy-800","children":"← TABE Reading Prep"}]]}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"container mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-10","children":[["$","section",null,{"className":"mb-12 rounded-2xl border border-eng-navy-200 bg-white p-6","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-display text-2xl font-bold text-eng-navy-900","children":"What the TABE Language test asks of you"}],[["$","p","Nearly half the test is Conventions of Standard English: sentence structure, verbs, pronouns, modifiers, capitalization, punctuation, and spelling. Another quarter is vocabulary — word meaning from context, word parts, and figurative language. The final quarter is a writing strand: introducing a topic, supporting it, and organizing what you say.",{"className":"mt-3 max-w-[70ch] text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":"Nearly half the test is Conventions of Standard English: sentence structure, verbs, pronouns, modifiers, capitalization, punctuation, and spelling. Another quarter is vocabulary — word meaning from context, word parts, and figurative language. The final quarter is a writing strand: introducing a topic, supporting it, and organizing what you say."}],["$","p","That last quarter is why this course has a writing strand at all. A test that devotes 25 percent of its Language section to writing is not testing whether you can name a comma splice; it is testing whether you can produce clear prose on demand.",{"className":"mt-3 max-w-[70ch] text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":"That last quarter is why this course has a writing strand at all. A test that devotes 25 percent of its Language section to writing is not testing whether you can name a comma splice; it is testing whether you can produce clear prose on demand."}]],["$","dl",null,{"className":"mt-6 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2","children":[["$","div","What it measures",{"className":"rounded-xl bg-eng-navy-50 p-4","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-eng-navy-500","children":"What it measures"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"mt-1 font-semibold text-eng-navy-900","children":"Grammar, usage, mechanics, vocabulary, and writing"}]]}],"$La","$Lb","$Lc"]}],"$Ld"]}],"$Le","$Lf","$L10","$L11","$L12"]}]]}],null,"$L13"]}]
