29:["$","span",null,{"children":"After should, could, would, and must, use have plus the participle, never of."}]
2a:["$","li","Check for a tense shift across a compound: he opened the drawer and finds the key changes time for no reason.",{"className":"flex gap-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-bold text-eng-teal-700","aria-hidden":"true","children":[4,"."]}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Check for a tense shift across a compound: he opened the drawer and finds the key changes time for no reason."}]]}]
2b:["$","div",null,{"className":"border-t border-eng-navy-100 bg-eng-navy-50/50 p-5","children":[["$","h4",null,{"className":"mb-3 text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-eng-navy-500","children":"Two worked examples"}],["$","ol",null,{"className":"grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"rounded-xl border border-eng-navy-200 bg-white p-4","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm font-semibold leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-900","children":"We should have ___ the form before submitting it. (reviewed / review / reviewing)"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-600","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-eng-navy-400","children":"Thinking"}]," ","— ","Should have is always followed by a past participle. Review is the base form and reviewing is a participle of the wrong kind."]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 rounded-lg bg-eng-green-50 p-2.5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-green-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-bold uppercase tracking-wide","children":"Answer"}]," ","— ","reviewed. The test uses this pattern often because should of is so common in speech."]}]]}],["$","li","1",{"className":"rounded-xl border border-eng-navy-200 bg-white p-4","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm font-semibold leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-900","children":"Which contains a tense shift? (A) He opened the drawer and found the key. (B) He opened the drawer and finds the key."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-600","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-eng-navy-400","children":"Thinking"}]," ","— ","B starts in the past with opened and jumps to the present with finds inside a single action. Nothing in the sentence justifies the change."]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 rounded-lg bg-eng-green-50 p-2.5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-green-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-bold uppercase tracking-wide","children":"Answer"}]," ","— ","B. Both verbs describe one moment, so both must be past."]}]]}]]}]]}]
2c:["$","span",null,{"children":"For pronoun case, remove the other person: the supervisor asked Maria and I becomes asked I, which is wrong."}]
2d:["$","li","For modifiers, check that the word right after an opening -ing phrase is the one doing that action.",{"className":"flex gap-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-bold text-eng-teal-700","aria-hidden":"true","children":[4,"."]}],["$","span",null,{"children":"For modifiers, check that the word right after an opening -ing phrase is the one doing that action."}]]}]
2e:["$","div",null,{"className":"border-t border-eng-navy-100 bg-eng-navy-50/50 p-5","children":[["$","h4",null,{"className":"mb-3 text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-eng-navy-500","children":"Two worked examples"}],["$","ol",null,{"className":"grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"rounded-xl border border-eng-navy-200 bg-white p-4","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm font-semibold leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-900","children":"The box of files ___ on the counter. (sit / sits)"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-600","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-eng-navy-400","children":"Thinking"}]," ","— ","Cross out of files. What remains is the box ___ on the counter. Box is singular."]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 rounded-lg bg-eng-green-50 p-2.5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-green-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-bold uppercase tracking-wide","children":"Answer"}]," ","— ","sits."]}]]}],["$","li","1",{"className":"rounded-xl border border-eng-navy-200 bg-white p-4","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm font-semibold leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-900","children":"Which is correct? (A) Walking into the office, the lights were already on. (B) Walking into the office, I saw that the lights were already on."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-600","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-eng-navy-400","children":"Thinking"}]," ","— ","In A the word after the opening phrase is lights, which claims the lights were walking. B puts the person doing the walking immediately after the comma."]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 rounded-lg bg-eng-green-50 p-2.5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-green-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-bold uppercase tracking-wide","children":"Answer"}]," ","— ","B. A is a dangling modifier — a favourite of this test because the sentence reads smoothly until you picture it."]}]]}]]}]]}]
