34:["$","span",null,{"children":"For word parts, split the word: pre-, re-, un-, -able, -tion. Then check the split against the sentence — word parts narrow the field but the context decides."}]
35:["$","li","Most nearly means is asking for the meaning in this sentence, not the dictionary's first entry.",{"className":"flex gap-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-bold text-eng-teal-700","aria-hidden":"true","children":[4,"."]}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Most nearly means is asking for the meaning in this sentence, not the dictionary's first entry."}]]}]
36:["$","div",null,{"className":"border-t border-eng-navy-100 bg-eng-navy-50/50 p-5","children":[["$","h4",null,{"className":"mb-3 text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-eng-navy-500","children":"Two worked examples"}],["$","ol",null,{"className":"grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"rounded-xl border border-eng-navy-200 bg-white p-4","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm font-semibold leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-900","children":"To keep the system stable, utilities ask large customers to curtail usage, reducing their draw voluntarily. Curtail most nearly means —"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-600","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-eng-navy-400","children":"Thinking"}]," ","— ","The sentence restates it immediately: reducing their draw. That is a definition clue sitting in the same sentence."]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 rounded-lg bg-eng-green-50 p-2.5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-green-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-bold uppercase tracking-wide","children":"Answer"}]," ","— ","to cut back. No outside knowledge of utilities is needed or wanted."]}]]}],["$","li","1",{"className":"rounded-xl border border-eng-navy-200 bg-white p-4","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm font-semibold leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-900","children":"The load on the grid climbs when air conditioners, ovens, and commuters all draw power at once. Load here means —"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-600","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-eng-navy-400","children":"Thinking"}]," ","— ","Load has a common meaning about transported goods, and the test will offer it. What follows the word defines it as simultaneous electricity use."]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 rounded-lg bg-eng-green-50 p-2.5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-green-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-bold uppercase tracking-wide","children":"Answer"}]," ","— ","the total demand for electricity. The familiar meaning is the distractor."]}]]}]]}]]}]
37:["$","li","For signal words, identify the relationship between the two ideas before you look at the choices: adding, contrasting, causing, comparing, illustrating, or sequencing.",{"className":"flex gap-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-bold text-eng-teal-700","aria-hidden":"true","children":[3,"."]}],["$","span",null,{"children":"For signal words, identify the relationship between the two ideas before you look at the choices: adding, contrasting, causing, comparing, illustrating, or sequencing."}]]}]
38:["$","li","Test your choice by reading both sentences with it in place. If the promise the word makes is not kept, it is the wrong word.",{"className":"flex gap-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-bold text-eng-teal-700","aria-hidden":"true","children":[4,"."]}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Test your choice by reading both sentences with it in place. If the promise the word makes is not kept, it is the wrong word."}]]}]
39:["$","div",null,{"className":"border-t border-eng-navy-100 bg-eng-navy-50/50 p-5","children":[["$","h4",null,{"className":"mb-3 text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-eng-navy-500","children":"Two worked examples"}],["$","ol",null,{"className":"grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"rounded-xl border border-eng-navy-200 bg-white p-4","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm font-semibold leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-900","children":"Grid operators describe August as walking a tightrope in the wind. This is an example of —"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-600","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-eng-navy-400","children":"Thinking"}]," ","— ","It is a direct comparison with no like or as, which makes it a metaphor rather than a simile. The next sentence explains it: a thin margin with immediate consequences."]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 rounded-lg bg-eng-green-50 p-2.5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-green-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-bold uppercase tracking-wide","children":"Answer"}]," ","— ","A metaphor, meaning that managing the grid requires fine balance under conditions that could upset it at any moment."]}]]}],["$","li","1",{"className":"rounded-xl border border-eng-navy-200 bg-white p-4","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm font-semibold leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-900","children":"Fare collection costs money to administer. ___, it slows boarding at every stop. (However / Furthermore)"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-600","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-eng-navy-400","children":"Thinking"}]," ","— ","Both sentences argue on the same side against fare collection. Nothing is being reversed, so a contrast word would mislead."]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 rounded-lg bg-eng-green-50 p-2.5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-green-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-bold uppercase tracking-wide","children":"Answer"}]," ","— ","Furthermore. However would promise a reversal the second sentence never delivers."]}]]}]]}]]}]
3a:["$","span",null,{"className":"font-bold text-eng-teal-700","aria-hidden":"true","children":[2,"."]}]
3b:["$","span",null,{"children":"For supporting detail, restate the claim in your own words first. Then test each choice against that claim, not against the topic generally."}]
3c:["$","li","For placement, look for the pronoun or transition in the sentence being moved — it usually points at what must come immediately before it.",{"className":"flex gap-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-bold text-eng-teal-700","aria-hidden":"true","children":[3,"."]}],["$","span",null,{"children":"For placement, look for the pronoun or transition in the sentence being moved — it usually points at what must come immediately before it."}]]}]
3d:["$","li","For a concluding sentence, rule out anything that merely repeats the opening, and anything that introduces a new idea the paragraph never developed.",{"className":"flex gap-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-bold text-eng-teal-700","aria-hidden":"true","children":[4,"."]}],["$","span",null,{"children":"For a concluding sentence, rule out anything that merely repeats the opening, and anything that introduces a new idea the paragraph never developed."}]]}]
3e:["$","li","For sentence combining, prefer the version that shows the relationship between the ideas rather than the shortest one.",{"className":"flex gap-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-bold text-eng-teal-700","aria-hidden":"true","children":[5,"."]}],["$","span",null,{"children":"For sentence combining, prefer the version that shows the relationship between the ideas rather than the shortest one."}]]}]
3f:["$","div",null,{"className":"border-t border-eng-navy-100 bg-eng-navy-50/50 p-5","children":[["$","h4",null,{"className":"mb-3 text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-eng-navy-500","children":"Two worked examples"}],["$","ol",null,{"className":"grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"rounded-xl border border-eng-navy-200 bg-white p-4","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm font-semibold leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-900","children":"A paragraph gives replacement costs, the difficulty of hiring exact skills, and what a certificate is worth to an employee. Which sentence best introduces it?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-600","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-eng-navy-400","children":"Thinking"}]," ","— ","Run the coverage test. A choice naming only replacement cost covers one third of the paragraph. A choice about employer generosity is contradicted by it. The right answer accounts for both the employer's reasons and the employee's gain."]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 rounded-lg bg-eng-green-50 p-2.5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-green-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-bold uppercase tracking-wide","children":"Answer"}]," ","— ","Employer-paid training is a practical exchange that benefits the company and the employee in different ways."]}]]}],["$","li","1",{"className":"rounded-xl border border-eng-navy-200 bg-white p-4","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm font-semibold leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-900","children":"Claim: midday clinic appointments fail because they compete with work shifts. Which detail best supports it?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-600","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-eng-navy-400","children":"Thinking"}]," ","— ","The unused-slot percentage shows that midday fails, but not why. The detail about patients losing pay if they leave a shift is the one that supports this specific claim."]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 rounded-lg bg-eng-green-50 p-2.5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-green-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-bold uppercase tracking-wide","children":"Answer"}]," ","— ","The detail about unpaid time off. A true fact that supports a different claim is the most common wrong answer on this question type."]}]]}]]}]]}]
